# The Dockerfile copies four things: requirements.txt, alembic.ini, alembic/
# and app/. Everything else in this directory is context the daemon copies
# across on every build and then throws away — .venv/ and node_modules/ alone
# are 113MB of the 116MB here.
#
# Written as an allow-list rather than a list of things to skip. A COPY added
# to the Dockerfile that this file has not been told about fails the build
# loudly and immediately; a deny-list that someone forgets to update fails by
# silently making builds slow again, which nobody ever notices.
*

!requirements.txt
!alembic.ini
!alembic
!app

# Re-excluded after the un-ignores above, which would otherwise sweep them
# back in. Stale bytecode compiled against the host's Python is worse than
# useless inside the image: it is the interpreter's cache of files it already
# has, keyed to a path and a version that may not match.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.DS_Store
